# Blueprints (trained model outputs) are git-ignored; the sibling
# analysis/abstractions/ (precompute inputs, e.g. bucket centroids) is committed.
backend/bot/analysis/blueprints/

# Baked postflop lookup tables are large (turn ~126MB) and fully regenerable
# from the committed centroids via scripts/bake_postflop_table.py, so they are
# git-ignored. Only the small centroids (the real inputs) are committed.
backend/bot/analysis/abstractions/postflop_table_*.npz

# Seed-compare baseline snapshot: a binary tied to the exact code+abstraction, so
# it goes stale on any abstraction change (sizing/bake/evaluator) and a check
# against a stale committed copy fails misleadingly. Regenerate on demand via
# `python tests/perf_seed_compare.py save perf_baseline.pkl`. Not committed.
backend/bot/perf_baseline.pkl

# Convergence-curve output from scripts/track_training.py -- a runtime data
# artifact that's rewritten every milestone; regenerated by the tracker, not
# committed.
backend/bot/analysis/training_curve.csv

# Cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc